Third-party software
The file connector application (its jar, container image and any distribution archive) includes third-party
software. Each bundled component, its license(s), its copyright line and its own NOTICE text are listed in
THIRD-PARTY.txt, and the license texts are in licenses/: under META-INF/ in the application jar, and in /app/legal/
in the container image. Where a component is offered under a choice of licenses, all of them are listed, and the
"Elected license" line names the one Smile Digital Health Inc. distributes it under: a permissive license (MIT,
Apache, BSD, ISC or Creative Commons) over any GNU General Public License or similar license.

The library jars (connector-contract, connector-core, connector-kms, connector-queue-reader) contain only Smile
Digital Health code, apart from the HL7-derived model described below; their third-party dependencies are declared
in their Maven POMs and are not included in them.

The distribution archive contains no Java runtime. The container image also contains:
- native libraries from zstd-jni (BSD-2-Clause) and snappy-java (Apache-2.0) in /app/native, so they can load
  from a read-only filesystem; both components are listed in THIRD-PARTY.txt;
- the Eclipse Temurin Java runtime (GPL-2.0 with the Classpath Exception, and others) and the operating system
  packages of its base image, listed with their versions and source packages in /app/legal/os-packages.txt. Each
  package's copyright and license terms are in the copyright file named there, under /usr/share/doc/.

HL7 Clinical Document Architecture
The C-CDA element model in connector-core (com/sdh/healthcare/connector/core/convert/cda-r2-sdtc.model) is
derived from the HL7 CDA Release 2 and SDTC XML schemas published by Health Level Seven International
(https://github.com/HL7/CDA-core-2.0, commit e922fc35586fd2629f0c8a021080bca9ab424e18). HL7 and CDA are registered
trademarks of Health Level Seven International. HL7 standards are used in accordance with the HL7 Intellectual
Property Policy (https://www.hl7.org/legal/ippolicy.cfm).
